discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Critical]** Authentication token (`?token=`) is no longer stripped from the browser URL after being consumed — Failure scenario: a user opens the web shell via `?token=SECRET` (the backward-compatible query-param path still supported by `getDaemonToken()`). With both `removeDaemonTokenFromUrl()` in `main()` and `url.searchParams.delete('token')` here removed, the token persists in the address bar, browser history, server access logs (query strings are part of the HTTP request line), and `Referer` headers on external link clicks. The PR description's security rationale ("the normal flow uses a URL fragment") only applies to `#token=`, not to `?token=`. The `sessionStorage` persistence already in place suffices for page refresh without keeping the token in the URL.

```suggestion
  if (!import.meta.env.DEV) {
    url.searchParams.delete('token');
    url.searchParams.delete('daemon');
  }
```

<details>
<summary>中文说明</summary>

**[Critical]** 认证 token（`?token=`）在读取后不再从浏览器 URL 中移除 — 失败场景：用户通过 `?token=SECRET`（`getDaemonToken()` 仍然支持的向后兼容 query 参数路径）打开 Web Shell。由于 `main()` 中的 `removeDaemonTokenFromUrl()` 和此处的 `url.searchParams.delete('token')` 均被移除，token 会保留在地址栏、浏览器历史记录、服务器访问日志（query 字符串是 HTTP 请求行的一部分）以及外部链接点击时的 `Referer` 头中。PR 描述中的安全理由（"常规流程使用 URL fragment"）仅适用于 `#token=`，不适用于 `?token=`。现有的 `sessionStorage` 持久化已足够支持页面刷新，无需将 token 保留在 URL 中。

</details>

